#X text 240 83 A non-interpolating sound generator based on the standard
map (also known as the Chirikov–Taylor map) \, a two-dimensional discrete
dynamical system. Unlike interpolating generators \, this object advances
the map by one step per audio sample at a given generation frequency.
The generation frequency is set as an audio signal on the first inlet
\, the minimal value is 0.001 Hz.;
#X text 240 199 The map is defined by the difference equations:;
#X text 240 224 y(n+1) = (y(n) + k * sin(x(n))) mod 2π;
#X text 240 249 x(n+1) = (x(n) + y(n+1)) mod 2π;
#X text 240 274 The parameter k is controlled by an audio signal on
the second inlet. For small k (roughly k < 1) the trajectories are
mostly regular (quasi-periodic or periodic) \, while for larger k the
system becomes increasingly chaotic.;
